<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hamilcar Barca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 275–228 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcid-family">Barcid family</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hamilcar Barca was a Carthaginian general who commanded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in the last years of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-punic-war">First Punic War</a> and then crushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary-war">Mercenary War</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. In 237 BCE he led an army to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, where he conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalquivir">Guadalquivir</a> valley and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines and founded a Carthaginian domain. He drowned in 228 BCE; his son-in-law Hasdrubal and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> continued his work.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hamilcar-barca.jpg" alt="Hamilcar Barca" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Max Karl Baldamus · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amilcare_Barca_(Ritratto).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Hamilcar Barca</b>, then Hasdrubal the Fair, founder of Qart Hadasht (Cartagena), and from 221 BCE Hannibal conquered the Iberians south of the Ebro, and Hannibal’s siege of Saguntum, an ally of Rome, began the Second Punic War.</blockquote><a href="/culture/iberians">Iberians · Contact &amp; Exchange</a></li><li><blockquote>After losing Sicily in the First Punic War, Carthage sent <b>Hamilcar Barca</b> to Iberia in 237 BCE.</blockquote><a href="/state/barcid-iberia">Barcid Iberia</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/tunisia">Tunisia</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jucar">Júcar</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=36.85,10.31&amp;year=-245" aria-label="Carthage on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4809 836 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Hamilcar Barca"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5259 1106h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5259 1106h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=36.85,10.31&amp;year=-245">What was here in 245 BCE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
